# PeraPera — Cursor AI rules

PeraPera is a Japanese learning app for serious JLPT learners. Read
`docs/PROJECT.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DESIGN.md`,
`docs/ROADMAP.md`, `docs/DATA.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md` for full context.
Below are the short imperative rules. When uncertain, the docs win.

## Stack — don't change without flagging

- Expo (managed) + expo-router + TypeScript (strict)
- Zustand for state, react-native-reanimated for animation
- react-native-svg, @expo/vector-icons (Ionicons)
- Plain React Native `StyleSheet` (no NativeWind)
- Python (stdlib only) for the data pipeline in `scripts/`

## File layout — respect it

- `app/_layout.tsx`        root layout + font loading
- `app/index.tsx`          DeckBuilder
- `app/study.tsx`          StudySession (prompt + reveal)
- `app/summary.tsx`        SessionSummary
- `src/theme.ts`           design tokens — SINGLE source of truth
- `src/types.ts`           data model
- `src/store.ts`           Zustand store
- `src/meta.ts`            POS / category display metadata
- `src/ui.tsx`             shared components (Chip, SectionHeader, Pill, Ring)
- `src/srs.ts`             ONLY shuffle() — SRS engine intentionally removed
- `src/LessonBlocks.tsx`   the lesson block-chip selector
- `src/data/vocab.json`    bundled vocab data
- `src/data/vocab.ts`      typed re-export
- `scripts/*.py`           data pipeline + import script
- `docs/`                  the durable context — keep current

## Hard rules

- All user-facing text must be inside `<Text>`.
- Never hardcode colors or font names. Reference `theme.*` and `fonts.*`.
- Vocab data conforms to the `Vocab` interface in `src/types.ts`.
- SRS state (if it returns) is per-user runtime data — NEVER mix it into
  the vocab list. It lives in the store, keyed by `vocabId` + direction.
- Don't introduce new dependencies without flagging it explicitly.
- Don't break the data pipeline. If you change `Vocab` shape, also update
  `scripts/import_vocab.py`.

## Design rules

- Calm/editorial visual language — NOT gamified-cartoon. No celebrations,
  no streak flames, no emoji in UI strings.
- The accent color (`theme.accent`) marks the answer or focus. Don't use
  it as a generic "primary."
- Fixed positions over dynamic balance — empty slots stay empty; never
  let fields slide up to fill them.
- Prompt always at the top of the study card; answer always below, after
  a divider. Same color for prompt across stages.
- Same size for prompt and answer text; distinguished by color (ink vs
  accent), position, and a small "ANSWER" label.
- Two-button commitment (Don't recall / I know this) — no card flipping,
  no peek.
- Section headers can carry an optional right slot (used for the Lessons
  "Clear" button) — always in the layout, just toggle enabled state, so
  it never causes reflow.

## When generating new screens

- Match the existing visual style and the StyleSheet patterns already used.
- Use the shared components in `src/ui.tsx` rather than reinventing chips,
  section headers, etc.
- Prefer small, composable components.
- For non-trivial new interactions, sketch the design first (in
  chat.claude.ai if needed) before coding.

## When working with vocab data

- The CSV (`scripts/Vocabulary_with_conjugations.csv`) is the source of
  truth. Edit there, then re-run `scripts/import_vocab.py` to regenerate
  `vocab.json`.
- The `ReviewFlag` column marks instructor-review rows — never silently
  trust those rows in any auto-generated content downstream.
- The 5 unconjugated verbs need manual entry by an instructor — see
  `docs/DATA.md`.

## When AI-generating content (sentences, explanations, examples)

- Output is a FIRST DRAFT, not ship-ready. Plan for instructor review.
- Flag uncertain outputs explicitly.
- Don't pull from copyrighted textbooks. Original content only.

## What's deliberately NOT in the codebase yet (don't add without asking)

- Persistence (expo-sqlite) — comes next, per ROADMAP.md
- SRS engine — removed; if it returns, use `ts-fsrs`
- User accounts / cloud sync
- Audio
- Social features, leaderboards, rewards
- English glosses (data is Chinese-only for now)
- Multi-language (Korean / Chinese)

## Recurring temptations to push back on

- "Let's add streaks / XP" — no, that's Duolingo.
- "Let's add in-app chat" — Discord handles community.
- "Let's pull example sentences from the textbook" — never; legal risk.
- "Let's promise 100% accuracy on AI content" — instructors review first.
- "Let's add a new language" — Japanese first, validate, then expand.
